@prefix : <http://example.org/orexis/world/dispatcher#> .
@prefix courier: <http://example.org/orexis/courier#> .
@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix planning: <http://example.org/orexis/planning#> .

<> a planning:DesireGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  TWO DESIRES, and desires rather than wants: the dispatcher runs for good, asking at every
#  instant that every parcel stand where it is owed and that no cell hold two vans.
#
#  THE DELIVERY points at the domain's shape and the domain's estimate, as the courier's want
#  does. The shape targets every parcel, so the derivation mints one want PER PARCEL — two
#  instances in trouble are two wants, as two debts are — and each is searched on its own.
#
#  THE AVERSION is the world's own, since no domain says that two vans may not share a cell, and
#  it is authored as `planning:unmetWhen`, as #567 asks: the AVOIDED STATE itself, one select
#  whose rows are the vans sharing a cell, unmet where it yields a row (#892). It was a met-test
#  over a `sh:sparql` constraint — a shape named `apart` wrapping this same select — because on
#  the tree that shipped it `weigh` read `planning:metWhen` alone and an aversion so authored was
#  weighed in no ground. The select projects the cell as `?value`, the offending value, so each
#  witness says where the two stand; it says nothing of what it is about, so the want minted from
#  it is about both vans and named for neither, and a one-step plan — either van's drive — parts
#  them (`tests/test_dispatcher.py`). It is also the world's one STATE INVARIANT: weighed in every
#  possible world a search here weighs, and a world that newly puts two vans on a cell is refused
#  (#902), which is what keeps the two parcels' joint plan off the other van's cell.

:dispatcher planning:holds :every_parcel_delivered , :no_cell_holds_two_vans .

:every_parcel_delivered a planning:Desire ;
    rdfs:label "every parcel where it is owed" ;
    planning:metWhen courier:delivered ;
    planning:estimates courier:drivesOwed .

:no_cell_holds_two_vans a planning:Desire ;
    rdfs:label "no cell holds two vans" ;
    planning:unmetWhen :two_vans_on_one_cell .

:two_vans_on_one_cell
    sh:message "two vans stand on one cell" ;
    sh:select """PREFIX courier: <http://example.org/orexis/courier#>
        SELECT $this ?value WHERE {
            $this a courier:Van ;
                courier:at ?value .
            ?other a courier:Van ;
                courier:at ?value .
            FILTER(?other != $this)
        }""" .
